1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:02,160
This is TyFi:

2
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:05,520
parametric typhoon insurance for Filipino farmers,

3
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:06,960
built on Stellar.

4
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:08,400
In the next four minutes,

5
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:10,960
we run the whole pipeline live on testnet.

6
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:14,880
A farmer signs in with a passkey,

7
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:16,400
with no seed phrase.

8
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:19,280
The farming co-op governs the insurance vault

9
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:20,560
through a DAO.

10
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:22,000
When a typhoon hits,

11
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,400
an oracle proves the storm crossed a

12
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:26,640
payout threshold with a zero-knowledge proof,

13
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:29,120
the vault verifies that proof on-chain,

14
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:31,440
and the payout lands in the farmer's wallet.

15
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:34,880
We start with the wallet.

16
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:36,160
On the passkey page,

17
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:38,720
the farmer names the wallet and taps create.

18
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:40,560
The device creates a passkey,

19
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:42,640
and our factory contract deploys a smart

20
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:43,920
wallet bound to it.

21
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:45,440
There is no seed phrase,

22
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:47,520
and no private key in the browser.

23
00:00:47,520 --> 00:00:48,560
From here on,

24
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:50,640
every transaction is approved with the same

25
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:52,000
fingerprint or face,

26
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,880
and checked on-chain by the wallet's own __check_auth.

27
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:57,920
Here is the deployment on Stellar Expert.

28
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:03,840
The co-op funds the wallet and verifies

29
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:06,800
the farm through the vault's admin multisig.

30
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:09,360
The farmer then joins the reinsurance pool

31
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:10,800
as a liquidity provider,

32
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:14,240
and insures a rice farm in Eastern Visayas.

33
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:15,920
Each of those steps is signed with

34
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:18,400
the passkey and settled on testnet.

35
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:21,800
Now, governance.

36
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:23,080
In the DAO tab,

37
00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:25,000
the farmer's voting power is read straight

38
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,080
from their liquidity shares in the vault.

39
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:28,440
A new proposal is open,

40
00:01:28,440 --> 00:01:29,880
and the farmer votes for it.

41
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:31,560
The passkey signs the vote,

42
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:33,000
and the tally updates on-chain.

43
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,480
Quorum is 30% of all shares,

44
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:39,480
and premium changes need a 60% supermajority.

45
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:41,800
Earlier, the co-op passed proposal 6:

46
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:47,320
raise the Eastern Visayas premium multiplier to 125%.

47
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:49,240
It then sat in a 12-hour timelock,

48
00:01:49,240 --> 00:01:51,640
so members could react before anything changed.

49
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:55,560
The timelock is over.

50
00:01:55,560 --> 00:01:57,560
The co-op made this farmer a DAO

51
00:01:57,560 --> 00:01:59,960
executor, so the farmer taps finalize,

52
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:01,400
and signs with the passkey.

53
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:04,280
The DAO contract then calls the vault

54
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:04,840
contract directly.

55
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:08,200
The vault only accepts parameter changes from

56
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:08,760
its DAO.

57
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:10,200
In the invocation tree,

58
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:13,160
you can see the DAO calling update_premium_rate

59
00:02:13,160 --> 00:02:14,360
on the vault,

60
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:19,480
and the Eastern Visayas multiplier moving from 100 to 125.

61
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:23,560
Then the storm.

62
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,240
Typhoon Odette crosses Eastern Visayas,

63
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:29,960
and the oracle reads 172 km/h.

64
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:31,400
That number stays private.

65
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:33,000
The oracle signs the reading,

66
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,160
and generates a Groth16 proof that its

67
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:36,920
registered key signed a reading at or

68
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:39,960
above the 150 km/h band.

69
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:42,840
The vault rebuilds every public input itself:

70
00:02:42,840 --> 00:02:44,040
the oracle's key,

71
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:45,640
the typhoon, the region,

72
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:46,600
the band, and the damage.

73
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:51,080
It checks the proof with Soroban's BN254

74
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:54,120
pairing functions, in about 30M instructions,

75
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:56,280
and stores only the band.

76
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:57,720
With consensus recorded,

77
00:02:57,720 --> 00:02:59,000
the farmer claims,

78
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,720
and the vault pays 85% of the

79
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:03,160
coverage straight to the passkey wallet.

80
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:08,040
Forged proofs fail.

81
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:09,240
Change the damage,

82
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:10,920
the region, the wind band,

83
00:03:10,920 --> 00:03:12,120
or the oracle key,

84
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:14,200
and the pairing check rejects it.

85
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:17,080
The contract test suite covers each case.

86
00:03:17,080 --> 00:03:19,800
The same statement is also written in

87
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:23,400
Noir, and one oracle signature satisfies both circuits.

88
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:26,520
And admin calls now require the multisig,

89
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:29,160
closing a zero-threshold bypass we found this week.

90
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:33,840
Every step has a testnet transaction you

91
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:36,160
can open on Stellar Expert.

92
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:37,840
The contracts, the app,

93
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:40,320
the oracle and both circuits are open

94
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:42,320
source under the MIT license,

95
00:03:42,320 --> 00:03:44,240
with a replication guide to run all

96
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:45,680
of it yourself.

97
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:46,560
That's TyFi.
